      "writtenOn": "2026-05-05T08:09:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand the approach, but I\u0027m not sure this actually improves the heap pressure. Doesn\u0027t it mostly move the allocation somewhere else?\n\nBefore, with either the lambda or a named acknowledgement class, we had one small ack object per consumed record. With this approach, we avoid that object, but we now need to keep a map entry for every unacked record, mapping the event back to the Kafka ConsumerRecord.\n\nI\u0027m not convinced the second one is cheaper, and it also seems to make the lifecycle more complex. The broker now owns a growing map of unacked records. If a client never calls ack(event) or fails before acking, that entry stays around unless we add cleanup logic.\n\nI\u0027m not against the idea, but I\u0027d like to understand whether we know this actually reduces allocation/heap pressure.\n\nCan we discuss?",
      "parentUuid": "cc0ae49a_f45f6f8c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 185,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 185,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "57ab43d5ce7b521221ddfd0223c24fdcf2eba5aa",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "213adb55_53f1ff82",
        "filename": "src/main/java/com/gerritforge/gerrit/plugins/kafka/subscribe/KafkaEventNativeSubscriber.java",
        "patchSetId": 27
      },
      "lineNbr": 185,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015244
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-05T16:21:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tested this approach and it does not work unfortunately.\n\n`Event` does not override `equals() / hashCode() `;\n\nSo to have a successful lookup in the `ackRecords` we would need to have _the same event instance (by id)_, but, this is not possible because, if we did that, we would still close over the context.\n\nAn alternative would be to change the new interface to something like:\n\n```\nvoid accept(T t, MessageAcknowledgement\u003cK\u003e acknowledgement);\n```\n\nThis would allow us to ack by `offset + partition` for example, bypassing the `event` comparison problem.\n\nI don\u0027t like this solution though, I think it is making the interface unnecessarily complex, to fix a problem that, frankly we don\u0027t really know we have yet.\n\nPerhaps we should spend more time in profiling this and making sure this optimisation is necessary?",
      "parentUuid": "e34ddf63_8aa86d84",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 185,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 185,
        "endChar": 84
      },
